//
// PROBE: the backtick PTR grammar term.
// Pins: reference/bund_language_parser/bund.pest:29 (the `ptr` production),
//       reference/bund_language_parser/src/vm/ptr.rs:7-10 (its handler).
// Why:  `ptr` is one of the twelve alternatives in `value` (bund.pest:7-20)
//       and `name` carries a negative lookahead !("`") at bund.pest:28 to
//       reserve the character for it. Zero corpus programs use it — every
//       backtick in the corpus sits inside a comment or a markdown literal.
//

:Greet {
  "probe: backtick ptr reached the word" println
} register

// Push a PTR naming the word, without invoking it, then execute it.
`Greet !
